200); Polypropylene: T50, T30\". Hmm, the original: \"For liner PTFE - T90; T50; T30\\nFor liner Rilsan - T50; T30 from DN50\\nFor liner Ebonite - T50; T30 from DN200\\nFor liner polypropylene - T50; T30\". I'll keep as a single string value.\n- water_pressure_class: \"MAP16\"\n- reverse_flow: \"designed to measure\"\n- environmental_class: \"O\" — and temperature range -25 to +55 °C. Record: environmental_class: {value: \"O\"} and environmental_class_temperature_range: {value: {min: -25, max: 55}, unit_symbol: \"°C\"}. The original text: \"O ( -25 to + 55 °C )\". Good.\n- electromagnetic_environment: \"E1, E2\" — could be a list [\"E1\", \"E2\"]. Value as string \"E1, E2\" or array. Structured value shape says value: number | {min,max} | string. I'll use string \"E1, E2\". Hmm, or maybe list not allowed. Keep string.\n- mechanical_class: \"B, O\"\n- maximum_admissible_temperature: PTFE 90 °C; Polypropylen/Rilsan/Ebonite 50 °C — varies by liner material. config_level? axis \"liner_material\": values: PTFE → 90, others → 50. I could do config_level with axis \"liner_material\". Conditions: \"PTFE\", \"Polypropylene, Rilsan, Ebonite\". That's nice.\n- maximum_admissible_pressure: 1.6 MPa\n- orientation_limitation: \"any\"\n- indicating_range: 9 999 999 m³ → value 9999999, unit m³\n- resolution_of_indicating_device: 0.01 m³\n- resolution_of_device_for_rapid_testing: \"-\" → omit (empty).\n- eut_test_category: \"Electromagnetic water meter\"\n- eut_test_case: \"Case D\" — string \"D\"? The original \"Case D\". Value: \"D\". I'll use \"D\".\n- connection_type: \"Flanged\" (screw thread — actually it says \"Connection type (screw thread): Flanged\" — a bit contradictory but keep value \"Flanged\")\n- minimum_straight_length_inlet_pipe: 0 mm\n- minimum_straight_length_outlet_pipe: 0 mm\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_class: \"U0D0\"\n- flow_conditioner: \"No\"\n- mounting: \"-\" omit\n- orientation: \"any\"\n- software_version: \"V.1.04.0005.0004\"\n- crc_checksum: \"9BA34F3B\"\n- cut_off: 0.2 % (value 0.2, unit \"%\")\n- detection_empty_pipe: \"on\"\n\nconfig_level:\nAxis 1: \"accuracy_class\"\n- mpe_lower_flowrate_zone: conditions \"class 1\" → 3 % (±3%), \"class 2\" → 5 %. Value shape: {condition, value, unit_symbol}. For ±3%, value could be 3 with a note that it's ±. Maybe value: 3, unit \"%\", and attribute name mpe_lower_flowrate_zone. The ± is implied by MPE. I'll just use the magnitude. Or keep string \"±3 %\". Structured value: value should be number where possible. MPE ±3% → value 3, unit_symbol \"%\". I think that's fine but loses the ±. Alternatively value: \"±3\". Hmm. I'll use number 3 with unit \"%\". Actually, to preserve fidelity, maybe keep as string \"±3 %\"? The rules push numbers. I'll do value: 3, unit_symbol: \"%\". Hmm, but percent as unit... rule example: \"0-15%vol\" → unit \"%vol\". For plain %, unit_symbol \"%\" seems fine.\n\n- mpe_upper_flowrate_zone_water_temp_le_30c: class1 → 1, class2 → 2, unit \"%\"\n- mpe_upper_flowrate_zone_water_temp_gt_30c: class1 → 2, class2 → 3, unit \"%\"\n\nAxis 2: \"liner_material\"\n- maximum_admissible_temperature: PTFE → 90 °C; \"Polypropylene, Rilsan, Ebonite\" → 50 °C\n\nAxis 3: \"power_supply_module\"\n- power_supply_voltage: HV → {min:100, max:240} V (type AC); LV → {min:24, max:36} V (AC/DC); LLV → {min:10, max:48} V (DC)\n- power_supply_type: HV → \"AC\"; LV → \"AC/DC\"; LLV → \"DC\"\n- power_supply_frequency: HV → {45,66} Hz; LV → {45,66} Hz; LLV → null/omitted\n- internal_backup_source: HV → \"3.7 V DC; 5200 mAh; Battery\"; LV → same; LLV → omitted\n\nFor config_level value shape: {condition, value, unit_symbol} per rule 5. And footnote_markers optional.\n\nAlternatively, since power module voltage/frequency vary, maybe better as config_level entries with axis \"power_supply_module\":\n\n{\n  \"attribute\": \"power_supply_voltage\",\n  \"axis\": \"power_supply_module\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"MS2500 / MV110 HV\", \"value\": {\"min\": 100, \"max\": 240}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"MS2500 / MV110 LV\", \"value\": {\"min\": 24, \"max\": 36}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"MS2500 / MV110 LLV\", \"value\": {\"min\": 10, \"max\": 48}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nAnd power_supply_type separate:\n{\"condition\": \"MS2500 / MV110 HV\", \"value\": \"AC\"}, {\"condition\": \"... LV\", \"value\": \"AC/DC\"}, {\"condition\": \"... LLV\", \"value\": \"DC\"}\n\nFrequency:\nHV: {45,66} Hz; LV: {45,66} Hz; LLV: omit (\"-\").\n\nInternal backup source: string \"3.7 V DC; 5200 mAh; Battery\" for HV and LV; LLV omit. Note original \"3,7V DC\" → decimal fix → 3.7 V DC. It's a compound string; keep as string with decimal fixed: \"3.7 V DC; 5200 mAh; Battery\".\n\nAlso I might break internal backup source into voltage/capacity/source but it's fine as string.\n\nComponents: power supply modules. I'll add:\n\ncomponents: [\n  {\n    \"role\": \"power supply module\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"MS2500 / MV110 HV\", \"MS2500 / MV110 LV\", \"MS2500 / MV110 LLV\"],\n    \"alternatives\": \"OR\"\n  }\n]\n\nAccuracy class axis config for MPE — note accuracy class is also a model attribute. Config axis \"accuracy_class\" conditions \"class 1\"/\"class 2\".\n\nNow footnotes: none in this fragment.\n\nrevision_history: none. test_reports: none (EUT testing requirements mention R 49-2:2013 8.1.8 — that's a reference, not a test report; but could note recommendation R49-2? No, that's just cited clause. I won't add test report.)\n\ncertificate: number \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-2022.02\", scheme \"A\". project_number? Not present. page_total: \"Page 10 of 16 pages\" and \"Page 11 of 16 pages\" → 16. Should I include page_total? It's present in the fragment (\"of 16 pages\"). Yes, page_total: 16. member_state: Czech Republic? The stamp says Český metrologický institut — member state Czechia. Hmm, \"CZ1\" in cert number. I could include member_state: \"Czech Republic\". Is that fabrication? It's a reasonable inference from the stamp, but strictly the country name isn't stated. The issuer is the Czech Metrological Institute. I'll include member_state: \"Czech Republic\" — hmm, borderline. I'll include it since ČMI is the Czech national metrology institute and the cert code CZ1 confirms. Actually to be safe, maybe omit member_state and just include issuing_authority.name. The fragment stamp: \"Český metrologický institut\". I'll include member_state: \"Czech Republic\" — I think that's justified. Let me include it.\n\ndate_issued: not present in fragment. Omit.\n\nissuing_authority:\n- name: \"Český metrologický institut\"\n- oiml_issuer_id: not given. Omit.\n\nActually wait — should I include issuing_authority at all based only on a stamp? The instruction says extract content present. The stamp is content. Include name only.\n\ncertified_type:\n- category: \"Water meter\"\n- type_designations: [\"MS2500 / MV110\"]\n- description: maybe \"Electromagnetic water meter\" — I have that in characteristics as measuring_principle. Could also set description. I'll set description: \"Electromagnetic water meter\" and keep type_level measuring_principle too? Redundant. I'll keep measuring_principle in type_level and omit description. Or include description. Hmm. I'll include description: \"Electromagnetic water meter\" — fine, both places. Actually keep it simple: type_level.measuring_principle. And certified_type.description omitted.\n\nmodel_family:\n- family_name: \"MS2500 / MV110\"\n- models: 6 entries with model_id and label.\n\nModel entries:\n{\"model_id\": \"DN200_Q3Q1=250\", \"label\": \"MS2500 / MV110 DN200, Q3/Q1=250, accuracy class 1\", \"attributes\": {\"nominal_diameter\": 200, \"q3_over_q1\": 250, \"accuracy_class\": 1}}? \n\nThe schema shows attributes{} as free-form. Maybe I'll just include model_id and label, and keep per-model values in model_level. I'll add light attributes for convenience. Hmm — duplication risk. I'll include model_id and label only, per-model values in model_level.\n\nActually, providing attributes in models is nice but duplicates model_level. The schema example shows attributes{} available. I'll include minimal attributes: nominal_diameter, q3_q1_ratio... Let me skip attributes to avoid bloat; model_level covers it. Hmm, but a consumer reading models[] alone wouldn't know. The label conveys it. OK.\n\nmatrix_tables: include the type details table. Also possibly the power supply table. Let me include both:\n\n1. name: \"Type details by nominal diameter and Q3/Q1 ratio\"\n   columns: [\"nominal_diameter\", \"q1\", \"q2\", \"q3\", \"q4\", \"q3_over_q1\", \"accuracy_class\", \"pressure_loss_class\", \"length\"]\n   Hmm, length is on page 11 with only 3 columns by DN. It fits the DN axis: DN200→350, DN250→450, DN300→500. I can include length in the same table per variant.\n   column_units: [\"mm\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null, null, null, \"mm\"]\n   rows: 6 rows as above with length.\n\n2. name: \"Power supply modules\"\n   columns: [\"module\", \"power_supply_type\", \"voltage_min\", ...]. Or rows as objects:\n   columns: [\"module_designation\", \"power_supply_type\", \"voltage\", \"frequency\", \"internal_backup_source\"]\n   column_units: [null, null, \"V\", \"Hz\", null]\n   rows:\n   - {module_designation: \"MS2500 / MV110 HV\", power_supply_type: \"AC\", voltage: {min:100, max:240}, frequency: {min:45, max:66}, internal_backup_source: \"3.7 V DC; 5200 mAh; Battery\"}\n   - {module_designation: \"MS2500 / MV110 LV\", power_supply_type: \"AC/DC\", voltage: {min:24, max:36}, frequency: {min:45, max:66}, internal_backup_source: \"3.7 V DC; 5200 mAh; Battery\"}\n   - {module_designation: \"MS2500 / MV110 LLV\", power_supply_type: \"DC\", voltage: {min:10, max:48}, frequency: null, internal_backup_source: null}\n\nOK. Let me now also think about q2_over_q1 = 1.6 and q4_over_q3 = 1.25 — type_level, dimensionless, unit null.\n\nMPE strings in the original:\n- \"±3 % (Class 1) / ±5 % (Class 2)\"