nNow model_level length: values per model:\nDN200 Q3/Q1=250 → 350\nDN200 Q3/Q1=400 → 350\nDN250 Q3/Q1=250 → 450\nDN250 Q3/Q1=400 → 450\nDN300 Q3/Q1=250 → 500\nDN300 Q3/Q1=400 → 500\n\nAll with unit \"mm\".\n\nAlso indicating_range: 9999999 m³ — value 9999999, unit \"m³\".\nresolution_of_indicating_device: 0.01 m³.\n\nWater pressure class MAP16 → string \"MAP16\". Could also add maximum_admissible_pressure 1.6 MPa (given).\n\nEnvironmental class: \"O\" with range -25 to +55 °C.\n\nNow certificate object:\n{\n  \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-2022.02\",\n  \"scheme\": \"A\",\n  \"page_total\": 16,\n  \"member_state\": \"Czech Republic\"\n}\n\nWait, scheme A — the number format \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-2022.02\": scheme letter is \"A\". Yes.\n\nShould I include oiml_issuer_id? Not present. Omit.\n\nrecommendation:\n{\n  \"id\": \"R49\",\n  \"edition\": 2013,\n  \"scheme\": \"A\",\n  \"accuracy_classes\": [1, 2]\n}\n\nThe R49 edition 2013 is evidenced by \"R49/2013\" and \"OIML R 49-2:2013\". Good.\n\nNote: R49 actually has parts; but id canonical \"R49\". Fine.\n\nLet me now double-check Q1 for DN250: row Q1: values 4.0, 2.5, 6.4, 4.0, 6.4, 4.0 → DN250 col3=6.4, col4=4.0. Yes.\n\nQ2: 6.4, 4.0, 10.2, 6.4, 10.2, 6.4.\n\nQ3: 1000, 1000, 1600, 1600, 1600, 1600.\n\nQ4: 1250, 1250, 2000, 2000, 2000, 2000.\n\nQ3/Q1: 250, 400, 250, 400, 250, 400.\n\nAccuracy class: 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2.\n\nConsistency: Q3/Q1: 1000/250 = 4? Wait Q3/Q1 = 250 means Q1 = Q3/250 = 1000/250 = 4.0 ✓. For 400: 1000/400 = 2.5 ✓. For 1600/250 = 6.4 ✓, 1600/400 = 4.0 ✓. \n\nQ2/Q1 = 1.6: 4.0×1.6=6.4 ✓; 2.5×1.6=4.0 ✓; 6.4×1.6=10.24→10.2 ✓.\n\nQ4/Q3=1.25: 1000×1.25=1250 ✓; 1600×1.25=2000 ✓.\n\nGreat.\n\nModel IDs — maybe include Q3 in the ID since it's the nominal flow: e.g., \"DN200 Q3=1000 Q3/Q1=250\". That's verbose. Simpler: \"DN200_Q3Q1=250\". I'll use \"DN200 Q3/Q1=250\" with spaces.\n\nNow, type_designations: The model number is \"MS2500 / MV110\". Possibly MS2500 is the meter and MV110 the converter? Doesn't matter. Type designations: [\"MS2500 / MV110\"].\n\nCut-off: \"0,2%\" → value 0.2, unit \"%\".\n\nDetection empty pipe: \"on\" → value true? or string \"on\". I'll use string \"on\"... hmm, boolean true might be nice. Schema: value: number | {min,max} | string. Keep \"on\"? I'll use \"enabled\"? Don't fabricate — keep \"on\".\n\nSoftware version: \"V.1.04.0005.0004\" string. CRC checksum: \"9BA34F3B\" string.\n\nEUT: category \"Electromagnetic water meter\", case \"D\".\n\nLet me also think about whether to put \"length\" per DN as config_level with axis nominal_diameter instead of model_level. Since models already split by DN, model_level is fine.\n\nNow decide structure ordering. Output JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-2022.02\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"member_state\": \"Czech Republic\",\n    \"page_total\": 16\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Český metrologický institut\"\n  },\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Hemina SPA\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Via Piemonte 2\", \"Montagnana\", \"350 44 Italy\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"MS2500 / MV110\"]\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": \"MS2500 / MV110\",\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN200 Q3/Q1=250\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN200 Q3/Q1=400\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN250 Q3/Q1=250\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN250 Q3/Q1=400\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN300 Q3/Q1=250\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN300 Q3/Q1=400\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"components\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"power supply module\",\n      \"type_designations\": [\"MS2500 / MV110 HV\", \"MS2500 / MV110 LV\", \"MS2500 / MV110 LLV\"],\n      \"alternatives\": \"OR\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {\n      \"q2_over_q1\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null},\n      \"q4_over_q3\": {\"value\": 1.25, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null},\n      \"measuring_principle\": {\"value\": \"Electromagnetic water meter\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null},\n      \"temperature_class\": {\"value\": \"PTFE liner: T90; T50; T30. Rilsan liner: T50; T30 (from DN50). Ebonite liner: T50; T30 (from DN200). Polypropylene liner: T50; T30\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null},\n      \"water_pressure_class\": {\"value\": \"MAP16\", ...},\n      \"pressure_loss_class\": {\"value\": \"Δp40\", ...},\n      \"reverse_flow\": {\"value\": \"designed to measure\", ...},\n      \"environmental_class\": {\"value\": \"O\", ...},\n      \"environmental_class_temperature_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -25, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\", ...},\n      \"electromagnetic_environment\": {\"value\": \"E1, E2\", ...},\n      \"mechanical_class\": {\"value\": \"B, O\", ...},\n      \"maximum_admissible_pressure\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\"},\n      \"orientation_limitation\": {\"value\": \"any\"},\n      \"indicating_range\": {\"value\": 9999999, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"},\n      \"resolution_of_indicating_device\": {\"value\": 0.01, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"},\n      \"eut_test_category\": {\"value\": \"Electromagnetic water meter\"},\n      \"eut_test_case\": {\"value\": \"D\"},\n      \"connection_type\": {\"value\": \"Flanged\"},\n      \"minimum_straight_length_inlet_pipe\": {\"value\": 0, \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\"},\n      \"minimum_straight_length_outlet_pipe\": {\"value\": 0, \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\"},\n      \"flow_profile_sensitivity_class\": {\"value\": \"U0D0\"},\n      \"flow_conditioner_required\": {\"value\": \"No\"},\n      \"orientation\": {\"value\": \"any\"},\n      \"software_version\": {\"value\": \"V.1.04.0005.0004\"},\n      \"crc_checksum\": {\"value\": \"9BA34F3B\"},\n      \"cut_off\": {\"value\": 0.2, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n      \"detection_empty_pipe\": {\"value\": \"on\"}\n    },\n    \"model_level\": [...],\n    \"config_level\": [...]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [...],\n  \"recommendation\": {...}\n}\n\nShould each characteristic value object include unit_id? The strict shape shows unit_id. Rule says \"Leave unit_id: null unless you are certain\". I'll include unit_id: null everywhere for shape compliance. That adds verbosity but follows \"STRICT\" shape. Yes, include unit_id: null in all.\n\nHmm — but for type_level, the schema example in system prompt shows `<label>: {value, unit, footnote_markers[]}`. The strict rule 2 says every value MUST be object with value, unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers. I'll include all keys: value, unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers (empty array or omit?). The shape shows footnote_markers in the object. For values without footnotes, include empty array? Example in rule 7 shows footnote_markers only when referenced. I'll include footnote_markers: [] where none... Actually the R60 example output shows values without footnote_markers ({\"model\": \"Emax=25t\", \"value\": 25}). For type_level, I'll include footnote_markers: [] to be consistent with the strict shape. Hmm, it bloats. The strict rule shows the shape including footnote_markers: [\"1)\"]. I think including \"footnote_markers\": [] is safest. But it doubles size. Let me include it only when non-empty, and include unit_id: null always. Hmm.\n\nThe rule says \"Every characteristic value MUST be an object with this shape\" — shape includes footnote_markers key. I'll include footnote_markers: [] everywhere to strictly comply. Actually let me reconsider: the example JSON in rule 2:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"value\": <number | {min, max} | string>,\n  \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\" | \"V\" | \"kg\" | null,\n  \"unit_id\": \"u:degree_Celsius\" | null,\n  \"footnote_markers\": [\"1)\"]\n}\n```\n\nOK include footnote_markers: [] where none. I'll do that for type_level and config/model values. That's a lot of repetition but compliant.\n\nHmm, for model_level entries the R60 example shows {\"model\": \"Emax=25t\", \"value\": 25} without unit_sym