power_supply_voltage, axis \"power_supply_module\":\n   - {condition: \"MS2500 / MV110 HV\", value: {min:100, max:240}, unit_symbol: \"V\"}\n   - {condition: \"MS2500 / MV110 LV\", value: {min:24, max:36}, unit_symbol: \"V\"}\n   - {condition: \"MS2500 / MV110 LLV\", value: {min:10, max:48}, unit_symbol: \"V\"}\n\n2. power_supply_type, axis \"power_supply_module\":\n   - HV: \"AC\", LV: \"AC/DC\", LLV: \"DC\"\n\n3. power_supply_frequency, axis \"power_supply_module\":\n   - HV: {45,66} Hz, LV: {45,66} Hz (LLV omitted since \"-\")\n\n4. internal_backup_source, axis \"power_supply_module\":\n   - HV: \"3.7 V DC; 5200 mAh; Battery\", LV: same (LLV omitted)\n\nMPE config axis \"accuracy_class\":\n1. mpe_lower_flowrate_zone: class 1 → 3 %, class 2 → 5 %\n2. mpe_upper_flowrate_zone_water_temperature_at_or_below_30c: class 1 → 1 %, class 2 → 2 %\n3. mpe_upper_flowrate_zone_water_temperature_above_30c: class 1 → 2 %, class 2 → 3 %\n\nAttribute naming: rule 1 canonical snake_case. \"maximum_permitted_error_lower_flowrate_zone\"? Original uses \"Maximum permissible error\". I'll use mpe_lower_flowrate_zone? Better spelled out: \"maximum_permitted_error_lower_flowrate_zone\" hmm \"permissible\": \"maximum_permissible_error_lower_flowrate_zone\". Fine.\n\nLiner axis:\nmaximum_admissible_temperature, axis \"liner_material\":\n- {condition: \"PTFE liner\", value: 90, unit_symbol: \"°C\"}\n- {condition: \"polypropylene, Rilsan or Ebonite liner\", value: 50, unit_symbol: \"°C\"}\n\nmodel_level list:\n\n1. nominal_diameter (mm): all 6\n2. minimum_flowrate_q1 (m³/h): 4.0, 2.5, 6.4, 4.0, 6.4, 4.0\n3. transitional_flowrate_q2: 6.4, 4.0, 10.2, 6.4, 10.2, 6.4\n4. permanent_flowrate_q3: 1000, 1000, 1600, 1600, 1600, 1600\n5. overload_flowrate_q4: 1250, 1250, 2000, 2000, 2000, 2000\n6. q3_over_q1: 250, 400, 250, 400, 250, 400\n7. accuracy_class: 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 2\n8. length (mm): 350, 350, 450, 450, 500, 500\n\nAttribute names: q1, q2, q3, q4 or spelled? R137 example used qmax, qt, qmin. So