le_designation\", \"power_supply_type\", \"voltage\", \"frequency\", \"internal_backup_source\"]\ncolumn_units: [null, null, \"V\", \"Hz\", null]\nrows:\n- {\"module_designation\": \"MS2500 / MV110 HV\", \"power_supply_type\": \"AC\", \"voltage\": {\"min\": 100, \"max\": 240}, \"frequency\": {\"min\": 45, \"max\": 66}, \"internal_backup_source\": \"3.7 V DC; 5200 mAh; Battery\"}\n- {\"module_designation\": \"MS2500 / MV110 LV\", \"power_supply_type\": \"AC/DC\", \"voltage\": {\"min\": 24, \"max\": 36}, \"frequency\": {\"min\": 45, \"max\": 66}, \"internal_backup_source\": \"3.7 V DC; 5200 mAh; Battery\"}\n- {\"module_designation\": \"MS2500 / MV110 LLV\", \"power_supply_type\": \"DC\", \"voltage\": {\"min\": 10, \"max\": 48}, \"frequency\": null, \"internal_backup_source\": null}\n\nNow recommendation accuracy_classes: [1, 2].\n\nWait — R49 water meter accuracy classes are 1 and 2. ✓.\n\nShould certificate include scheme? yes \"A\".\n\nAlso \"project_number\": not present. Omit.\n\nmember_state: \"Czech Republic\" — hmm, I'll include; ČMI stamp + CZ1 code. Fine.\n\nLet me reconsider whether to include \"issuing_authority\". The stamp is described as \"[Blue round stamp, partly visible: \"Český metrologický institut\" ...]\". This is an image artifact description but contains the institution name. I'll include issuing_authority.name. \n\nOne more consideration: the fragment header shows the OIML Certificate No. table. Good, number captured.\n\nLabel \"Description of the module for all nominal diameter\" → power modules apply to all DNs. Captured in components/config.\n\nAlso \"Resolution of the device for rapid testing [m³]: -\" → omit.\n\n\"Mounting: -\" omit. \"Wiring instructions: -\" omit. \"Mounting arrangement: -\" omit. \"Orientation limitations: -\" (electrical) omit. \"Other relevant information: -\" omit.\n\n\"Flow conditioner (details if required): No\" → flow_conditioner: \"No\".\n\nNow write the final JSON. Ensure valid JSON: no trailing commas, escape nothing weird. Use Unicode °C, m³, Δ, Č directly.\n\nAlso include footnote_markers: [] in type_level entries. And unit_id: null.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-2022.02\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"member_state\": \"Czech Republic\",\n    \"page_total\": 16\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Český metrologický institut\"\n  },\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Hemina SPA\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Via Piemonte 2\", \"Montagnana\", \"350 44 Italy\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"MS2500 / MV110\"],\n    \"description\": \"Electromagnetic water meter, model MS2500 / MV110, nominal diameters DN200, DN250 and DN300.\"\n  },\n  ...\n}\n\nHmm — description includes inference \"DN200...\" fine, it's derived from the table. Or simpler: \"Electromagnetic water meter\". I'll keep it concise: \"Electromagnetic water meter\". Actually measuring_principle is in type_level. Description optional; I'll set \"Electromagnetic water meter\" — duplicates but harmless. Let me skip certified_type.description and keep measuring_principle in type_level. Actually I'll include description since schema lists it; a small description helps. I'll include: \"Electromagnetic water meter\". OK.\n\nmodel_family.family_name: \"MS2500 / MV110\".\n\nmodels: with labels:\n{\"model_id\": \"DN200 Q3/Q1=250\", \"label\": \"MS2500 / MV110 DN200, Q3=1000 m³/h, Q3/Q1=250, accuracy class 1\"} etc. That's nice detail. Include attributes? I'll skip attributes since matrix covers.\n\nActually, let me add attributes minimal: {\"nominal_diameter\": 200, \"q3_over_q1\": 250}. Eh. The label already says. Keep model_id + label only.\n\nComponents entry as planned.\n\ncharacteristics.type_level — final list:\n\n- \"q2_over_q1\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n- \"q4_over_q3\": {\"value\": 1.25, ...}\n- \"me